<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm on limited stocks.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm on limited stocks.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices firmed on Thursday on limited stocks with arrivals from central Indian areas falling due to rains, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said prices gained by 200-250 rupees per tonne on strong undertone.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were strong due to better demand at lower levels. Soyoil solvent rose by 200 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined was up by 100 rupees.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices firmed on good export demand but offerings were limited. Soymeal yellow was $264-265 per tonne in export for ready and November shipment. Rapeseed extraction was $118-119 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,050 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,000-4,025 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
